cat > README.md << 'EOF'
# RHEL LVM Storage Management Automation

A comprehensive Bash script to automate the full LVM (Logical Volume Manager)
lifecycle on Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL 8/9).

## Features

- Create Physical Volumes (PV), Volume Groups (VG), Logical Volumes (LV)
- Format LVs as ext4 or XFS filesystem
- Mount LVs with UUID-based persistent /etc/fstab entries
- Extend LVs online with automatic filesystem resize (resize2fs / xfs_growfs)
- Safely reduce ext4 LVs with pre-checks (e2fsck)
- Setup and persist swap space on LVs
- Extend Volume Groups by adding new disks
- Remove PV / VG / LV safely with confirmation prompts
- Auto-backup /etc/fstab before every modification
- All actions logged to /var/log/lvm_management.log

## Requirements

- RHEL 8 or RHEL 9
- lvm2 package (auto-installed by script if missing)
- Must run as root or with sudo

## Quick Start

```bash
chmod +x scripts/lvm_management.sh
sudo ./scripts/lvm_management.sh
```

## Testing Without a Physical Disk

```bash
chmod +x configs/loop-device-setup.sh
sudo ./configs/loop-device-setup.sh
# Then use /dev/loop10 and /dev/loop11 in the script
```

